1
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:19,000
Archer, I don't believe it. You—

2
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,730
You once asked me this, Saber:

3
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:26,850
"Have you no pride as a hero?"

4
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,970
Of course I don't.

5
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:35,190
All I have left is foolish regrets.

6
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,900
The thing is, Saber...

7
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:43,030
I should never have become a hero.

8
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,280
I suggest you stand aside, King of Knights.

9
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:53,790
If you exert yourself with no Master, you will quickly disappear.

10
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:58,780
Emiya Shirou is no longer a Master.

11
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:02,180
Aiding him will not help your wish come true.

12
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:10,680
I swore that I would be the sword that protected him.

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,840
Even without our contract, that pledge remains unchanged.

14
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:16,970
I see.

15
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:20,980
In that case...

16
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:54,450
{\an4}The Beginning of the Circle

17
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:20,950
Die here, along with your false master.

18
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:26,740
Oh?

19
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:29,360
I expected you to cower a bit longer.

20
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,720
Shut up!

21
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:32,200
You're fighting the wrong person!

22
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:39,360
Your imitation is close enough to effectively be the real thing.

23
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:44,130
But can your body handle that level of magical exertion?

24
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,800
Using magic beyond your ability will destroy you.

25
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:59,100
Or did you honestly think you would succeed?

26
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:04,600
That if you stubbornly kept trying,
your ideal self would come within your grasp?

27
00:04:08,370 --> 00:04:09,540
Archer...

28
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,140
That is as far as Emiya Shirou can go.

29
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:28,250
A fitting end for a fool who constantly tried to do the impossible.

30
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:32,540
I hereby propose.

31
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:37,930
Your fealty shall be mine, and my fate shall be yours.

32
00:04:37,930 --> 00:04:42,820
If you heed the Grail's call and obey my will and reason...

33
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,030
then obey me!

34
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:54,430
Do so, and I shall entrust my fate to your sword!

35
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:58,410
On my honor as Saber, I accept your oath.

36
00:04:58,790 --> 00:05:02,250
I accept you as my Master, Rin.

37
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,730
What will it be, Saber?

38
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,790
Now that you've made a contract with Rin,

39
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:27,520
your ties with Emiya Shirou have been well and truly severed.

40
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:29,930
Weren't you listening, Archer?

41
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,720
My pledge to Shirou stands.

42
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,320
And what will you do?

43
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:40,200
Surely you do not think you can defeat me as I am now.

44
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:47,040
How confident you've become
after simply having your mana restored.

45
00:06:03,890 --> 00:06:05,560
It's over, Archer.

46
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,910
Earlier, you voiced concern for my wellbeing,

47
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:11,860
but now I could say the same to you.

48
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,520
You have nothing to anchor you to this world.

49
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:19,740
And with no means of supplying yourself with mana, what can you do?

50
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:26,250
Servants of the Archer class
have the ability to act independently.

51
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:30,740
I think I can last two days or so without a Master.

52
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:34,500
More than enough time to put down that boy.

53
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:37,670
Ridiculous. Do you still refuse to let go of that obsession?

54
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,660
Are you saying your wish was never the Holy Grail,

55
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:43,100
but killing Shirou?

56
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:49,350
Archer, your wish is misguided.

57
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:53,610
Misguided, is it?

58
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:56,920
You took the words out of my mouth, Saber.

59
00:06:56,920 --> 00:07:00,740
How long will you cling to your own misguided wish?

60
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:04,240
Instead of lamenting your failure to leave a legacy,

61
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:08,750
why can't you look back and accept that you did all you could?

62
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:18,280
I am an archer.

63
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,930
I was never meant to fight using swords.

64
00:07:21,490 --> 00:07:22,960
Though admittedly...

65
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:27,350
My bow is just as much a borrowed forgery.

66
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,850
I'm saying that I will show you my true nature.

67
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:35,020
That is the greatest recompense that I can offer you.

68
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,780
I am the bone of my sword.

69
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,360
Stop, Archer!

70
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,740
I do not wish to...

71
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,820
Unknown to Death.

72
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:46,240
Nor known to Life.

73
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:50,460
Saber, one day someone will appear who will free you.

74
00:07:51,290 --> 00:07:55,920
But the sole objective of my current self is to kill Emiya Shirou.

75
00:07:56,410 --> 00:08:01,090
If you try to stand in my way,
this world will not show mercy, even to you.

76
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,260
Unlimited...

77
00:08:06,170 --> 00:08:08,100
Blade Works!

78
00:08:23,090 --> 00:08:25,330
A Reality Marble?

79
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:30,020
A forbidden spell that causes the caster's inner world to manifest itself and encroach on reality.

80
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:35,830
Which means that you aren't a swordsman or a bowman.

81
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:38,200
Correct.

82
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:43,090
Before I became a Heroic Spirit, I was a mage in life.

83
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:46,430
Then what is your Noble Phantasm, Archer?

84
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:51,990
I owned neither a holy sword nor a demonic one.

85
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:55,060
All I have is this world.

86
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:58,610
If a Noble Phantasm is a Heroic Spirit's symbol,

87
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:01,630
then this Reality Marble is my Noble Phantasm.

88
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:06,070
It reproduces and stores any weapon whose original I've seen.

89
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,910
That is my ability as a Heroic Spirit.

90
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:11,700
Then this...

91
00:09:12,470 --> 00:09:17,000
You're saying this desolate wasteland
is the culmination of your life's efforts, Archer?

92
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,570
You don't mince words.

93
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:21,840
Care to test it, Saber?

94
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:26,220
I'll faithfully replicate that holy sword of yours.

95
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,560
My holy sword?

96
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:32,590
Yes. It is a projection that's certain to end in my destruction,

97
00:09:32,590 --> 00:09:35,240
but I can produce a convincing replica.

98
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,730
It should last long enough to take you with me.

99
00:09:38,230 --> 00:09:41,540
However, when two holy swords clash,

100
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:44,650
who can say whether any humans in the vicinity will survive?

101
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:46,070
That son of a...

102
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:48,520
Feel free to dodge them.

103
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,580
But if you do, you will doom the man behind you.

104
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:53,830
Shirou?!

105
00:09:55,480 --> 00:10:00,880
If the rules and principles of all the copying I've done so far are right...

106
00:10:01,590 --> 00:10:02,380
Trace...

107
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:05,380
on!

108
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:09,740
Faster.

109
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,390
Better.

110
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:14,350
Stronger.

111
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:18,040
I understand the structure.

112
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:21,020
I'm sick of

113
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,530
your crap!

114
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:34,280
The Reality Marble's gone?

115
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,030
Why?

116
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,920
Archer, what do you think you're...

117
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,250
Tohsaka!

118
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:52,340
Where are you going, Archer?

119
00:10:52,870 --> 00:10:55,290
Back to the drawing board.

120
00:10:55,290 --> 00:10:57,970
After that gambit, I'm out of mana.

121
00:10:57,970 --> 00:11:00,850
I'm in no state to take you on at full strength.

122
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,820
This is simply my insurance policy.

123
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:07,850
If you value your Master's life, I suggest you stay out of this, Saber.

124
00:11:07,850 --> 00:11:10,090
My objective is that boy's—

125
00:11:10,090 --> 00:11:12,360
The forest outside of town.

126
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:13,480
What?

127
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:17,020
There's a castle there that's empty now.

128
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:17,860
Shirou?

129
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,800
You want to give me a piece of your mind?

130
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,840
Fine, let's hear it.

131
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:25,870
There are things I want to say to you too.

132
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:30,380
True, we won't be interrupted at that castle.

133
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:33,670
I like your resolve, Emiya Shirou.

134
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,010
Go to hell.

135
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:36,630
And don't you dare hurt Tohsaka.

136
00:11:36,630 --> 00:11:38,380
I'll kill you!

137
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,640
I'll guarantee her safety for one day.

138
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,340
Be quick, though.

139
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:47,140
I won't last longer than two days without a Master.

140
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,900
If I can't kill you by that time,

141
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:52,960
I might just dismember my hostage out of spite.

142
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:57,650
Shirou!

143
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,680
You're being reckless.

144
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:03,660
You're too inexperienced to attempt the same projections as Archer.

145
00:12:04,470 --> 00:12:06,890
Sorry, Saber.

146
00:12:06,890 --> 00:12:09,290
I let Tohsaka get captured.

147
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:13,200
Right now, you are in more danger than she is.

148
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,050
Let me worry about Rin.

149
00:12:15,050 --> 00:12:17,710
You should return home and rest.

150
00:12:28,970 --> 00:12:31,940
Looks like you took care of business, kid.

151
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,940
Hold on, Saber.

152
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:37,750
He helped us.

153
00:12:38,850 --> 00:12:41,860
Are you saying that Lancer assisted you, Shirou?

154
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,210
Yeah, he did.

155
00:12:44,210 --> 00:12:46,870
So try not to fight him for now, okay?

156
00:12:46,870 --> 00:12:48,510
Why, Lancer?

157
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:53,710
Do you have some ulterior motive in helping Shirou and Rin?

158
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,960
Of course I do.

159
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:00,630
You think I'd help my opponents if there was nothing in it for me?

160
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:02,670
I understand.

161
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:04,850
Meaning that you've gotten what you wanted.

162
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:06,170
Then begone.

163
00:13:06,170 --> 00:13:08,270
I won't fight you now, either.

164
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:14,350
Hey. It appears things didn't go entirely according to plan.

165
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,030
What happened in there, kid?

166
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,530
Tohsaka's been abducted by Archer.

167
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,750
This hill is his world—

168
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:32,630
the ultimate result of his unending quest to help people.

169
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:39,960
It seemed like he'd embraced this landscape
and died with a smile, saying he was satisfied.

170
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,570
Seriously? How stupid is that?

171
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:47,060
Anyway, that made me really angry.

172
00:13:48,590 --> 00:13:51,810
He worked and worked, striving for greatness
even though he was ordinary,

173
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,810
finally achieving his miracle as he bled.

174
00:13:56,410 --> 00:13:59,180
So it'd be unthinkable for him not to find his happiness.

175
00:13:59,930 --> 00:14:02,370
If he made lots of people happy,

176
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:07,850
he should become at least as happy as those people combined.

177
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:12,120
However, that wasn't the reward he received.

178
00:14:12,870 --> 00:14:14,330
Instead, all he got

179
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:18,960
was his exploitation as a Guardian, even after his death.

180
00:14:20,290 --> 00:14:23,380
Why did I never put it together?

181
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:27,190
Servants are summoned from every age.

182
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:34,600
Heroic Spirits can be summoned from the past, the present, or even the distant future.

183
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:37,800
Nothing says a Servant couldn't be summoned

184
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:41,650
into the time when he lived, to the city in which he once lived.

185
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:44,970
That thought frustrates me so much.

186
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:47,160
Because neither one will be saved.

187
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:50,210
Neither the one looking at his past self

188
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:52,250
nor the one looking at his future self.

189
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:56,750
All they can do is mourn what they've become.

190
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:03,750
I already know how it will end
for that fool who lives to help others.

191
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:08,150
He voluntarily sacrificed his afterlife.

192
00:15:08,850 --> 00:15:11,500
If he could keep saving people, even after death,

193
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,560
he could ask no more.

194
00:15:14,310 --> 00:15:17,400
Because of his powerlessness, he failed to save people in life.

195
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:21,520
So, thinking that he could avert
all kinds of tragedies as a Heroic Spirit,

196
00:15:22,530 --> 00:15:24,940
he sold the peace he would have found in death,

197
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:30,410
believing with all his heart
that he could save tens of thousands more lives.

198
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:34,120
But even that hope was betrayed.

199
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,940
Only one thing can be said about him:

200
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:42,590
that he has been constantly betrayed by everything around him.

201
00:15:43,070 --> 00:15:44,860
And at the very, very end,

202
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,930
he was betrayed even by the one ideal in which he believed.

203
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:04,440
What are you trying to pull, Archer?

204
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:11,700
Shirou would have come after you whether I was here or not.

205
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,500
You should know that better than anyone.

206
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,310
I suppose you're right.

207
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:20,210
But it would be inconvenient to have you in the way.

208
00:16:20,570 --> 00:16:21,630
I see.

209
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:25,220
Then you intend to kill Shirou, no matter what, don't you?

210
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:29,800
Yes, that naïve boy should be put down before it's too late.

211
00:16:31,270 --> 00:16:35,210
I don't need you to tell me that Shirou is naïve.

212
00:16:36,810 --> 00:16:41,650
But even so, I think his naïveté is sweet.

213
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,570
That's how he ought to be.

214
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,820
It gives me hope that he has a place in this world.

215
00:16:49,110 --> 00:16:51,030
But what about you?

216
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:52,570
After all you've done,

217
00:16:52,570 --> 00:16:56,370
did you decide that waving self-indulgent idealism in people's faces is wrong?

218
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:59,620
After fighting for others time and time again,

219
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:02,000
being betrayed time and time again,

220
00:17:02,310 --> 00:17:05,550
being forced to clean up other people's messes
time and time again...

221
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:06,780
Did you...

222
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:09,300
Did you lose your faith in humanity,

223
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,370
Archer?

224
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,810
I am the bone of my sword...

225
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:24,400
That's the incantation you were given
after you became a Heroic Spirit, right?

226
00:17:25,030 --> 00:17:26,790
What the hell?

227
00:17:26,790 --> 00:17:28,650
It's basically a curse.

228
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:34,360
I can't come to terms with one single thing about your life.

229
00:17:34,910 --> 00:17:37,040
Not your idiotic way of living,

230
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:39,260
nor the people around you who didn't set you straight.

231
00:17:40,050 --> 00:17:42,420
Try as I might,

232
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:45,020
I just can't come to terms with it.

233
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,830
What a surprise, Tohsaka!

234
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:55,800
I was skeptical, but you really are here.

235
00:17:58,430 --> 00:17:59,800
Shinji?

236
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,390
Visitors?

237
00:18:01,390 --> 00:18:03,710
I came here because I thought we wouldn't be disturbed.

238
00:18:03,710 --> 00:18:04,960
Hey, now.

239
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,880
No funny business, Archer.

240
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:10,480
I'm not interested in you.

241
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:15,990
In fact, I should warn you: you're outmatched.

242
00:18:20,070 --> 00:18:21,840
You're scared, aren't you, Archer?

243
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:26,250
My Servant dispatched Berserker without breaking a sweat.

244
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:28,500
I don't blame you for being scared of—

245
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:31,260
You want Rin, Matou Shinji?

246
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:34,460
Of course I do.

247
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,620
Then wait until my business is concluded.

248
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:40,180
Once I've finished Emiya Shirou, she's all yours.

249
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:45,190
If you won't agree to those terms,
I'll eliminate both you and your Servant.

250
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:47,940
Oh?

251
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:50,290
Hold on, Gilgamesh.

252
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:53,190
It's fine. He says he'll give her to us, so let's go along.

253
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:58,910
We'll keep Tohsaka safe until he's dealt with Emiya, okay?

254
00:18:58,910 --> 00:19:00,120
Which means...

255
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,400
She's already as good as mine, right?

256
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:05,370
So I can do anything I want to her, right?

257
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:09,710
My agreement with Emiya Shirou was that she'd remain unharmed.

258
00:19:09,710 --> 00:19:11,800
But that expires at dawn.

259
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:15,660
Once the deadline has passed, do as you will.

260
00:19:20,730 --> 00:19:22,850
Did you hear that, Tohsaka?

261
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:26,690
Your Servant's willing to sell out his Master!

262
00:19:31,730 --> 00:19:33,140
Faker.

263
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:47,350
Have you awoken,

264
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:49,580
Shirou?

265
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:54,320
Yeah, the fatigue's gone, and so is my headache.

266
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:57,350
My mana's still pretty depleted,

267
00:19:57,350 --> 00:20:00,680
but it doesn't seem like my magic circuits were burned out.

268
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:03,680
Shirou...

269
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,900
Rin is my Master.

270
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,870
Rescuing her is my duty.

271
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:12,180
I will stop Archer, so you—

272
00:20:12,180 --> 00:20:13,450
That's backwards, Saber.

273
00:20:14,070 --> 00:20:15,780
I'll handle the fight with Archer.

274
00:20:16,150 --> 00:20:17,860
You cannot, Shirou.

275
00:20:18,530 --> 00:20:20,120
Archer is your...

276
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,530
I know.

277
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:26,410
I've probably known who he was since the moment I met him.

278
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:29,920
All the more reason why I can't stand for what he's done.

279
00:20:31,010 --> 00:20:34,590
I have to be the one to settle things with him.

280
00:20:35,370 --> 00:20:38,010
Please. Let me fight Archer.

281
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:42,090
And when it happens, I want you to stay out of it, no matter what.

282
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:48,150
If that is your wish, I shall abide by it.

283
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,420
I swore that I would be your shield.

284
00:20:53,290 --> 00:20:56,480
As such, I shall watch over you to the very end.

285
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:59,550
Thanks, Saber.

286
00:21:07,070 --> 00:21:09,750
I'm surprised you don't have better things to do.

287
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:12,750
I've changed my mind.

288
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:15,530
The little lady's in trouble, right?

289
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:18,700
So let me tag along a bit longer.

290
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,760
I couldn't sleep at night if I left her.

291
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:26,590
What manner of magic did you and Rin use
to bring him over to your side?

292
00:23:10,030 --> 00:23:13,070
Ryuudou Temple, Miyama. Fifty-three unconscious.

293
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:14,370
All male.

294
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,980
Low blood pressure, labored breathing.

295
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:19,630
Identical symptoms to the other coma patients.

296
00:23:19,630 --> 00:23:24,090
Send thirty-one to Shinto's general hospital, fifteen to the central hospital,

297
00:23:24,090 --> 00:23:26,540
and the rest to the community hospital.

298
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:42,360
Wasn't it my Master's credo to never reveal themselves?

299
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:44,360
There can't be two of those pendants.

300
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:47,130
Why would your own ideal reject you?

301
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:48,880
I'm leaving this fight before you.

302
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:52,660
THE ANSWER

303
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:52,660
Idealism's End

304
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:52,660
Next Time

305
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:51,270
In any event, you have no future.

